# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.coverage

# Secrets — never commit tokens (HF_TOKEN_WRITE, GH_TOKEN, VAST_API_KEY)
.env
.env.*
*.token
secrets.sh

# Training artifacts (checkpoints go to the HF Hub, not git)
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.gguf
data/shards/
data/shards-*/
*.npy
*.memmap

# Local tooling / OS
.DS_Store
.deepeval/

# Agent-local Claude Code settings and scratch worktrees. Machine-local by
# construction -- they configure the agent session running on *this* box, not
# the project -- so a committed copy would silently reconfigure someone else's
# session, and `.claude/worktrees/` holds whole nested checkouts.
.claude/

# W&B local run cache — already synced to the cloud, don't bloat git history
wandb/

# Live process pidfiles — pure ephemeral process-tracking, dead the moment
# the run ends; an automated checkpoint commit swept a stale one into git
# once already (see STATUS.md "Fourth incident" / 74e519b)
runs/**/*.pid

# The Hub upload queue. `*.pt` already keeps the 321 MB payloads out, but the
# `.upload.json` sidecars slipped through on abl-arch's first staged
# checkpoint. They are transient by construction — ckpt_uploader deletes each
# one the moment its payload lands on the Hub — so a committed sidecar is at
# best noise and at worst a resurrected instruction to re-upload a file that
# no longer exists.
runs/**/hub_outbox/

# Top-level dataprep run-tracking manifests and logs -- rewritten continuously
# during a run and can go stale/misleading (a --resume run reads this to
# decide what's already "done"); a wip commit swept a stale one into git
# once already (see STATUS.md "Housekeeping" note after the 4th dataprep
# attempt). Per-source shard manifest.json under data/shards-*/ is already
# covered by that pattern above.
data/manifest-*.json
runs/*/dataprep.log
runs/*/monitor*.log
runs/*/sweep.log
runs/*/sweep_watch.log

# Regenerated on demand by scripts/gguf_task_delta.py from eval.load_hellaswag,
# so the 7.5 MB is derived, not source. Keeping it out also keeps the item set
# honest: it must come from the same loader eval.py scores peers with, never
# from a stale checked-in copy that has drifted from the harness.
data/eval/hellaswag-llamacpp.txt

# credit_watch runtime state: the last verdict (so an issue is filed once)
# and the last-written signature (so STATUS.md is not rewritten every poll).
# Local to the box by design -- neither belongs in history.
runs/.credit-watch-verdict
runs/.credit-watch-verdict.sig

# Stray artifacts from tests that use the run-name "test" (tests pass an
# isolated run_dir, but a future one might not). No real run is named "test":
# they are hero, sweep-*, abl-arch-*, post-*.
runs/test/

# Boot-resume state is machine-local by nature: `inflight.json` says "a trainer
# is running on THIS box right now". Committed, it could be restored into a
# fresh clone (workspace_is_volume is False, so a recycle re-clones) and tell
# `scripts/boot_resume.py` to continue a run that never started here -- which,
# with no checkpoint present, means launching `hero` from step 0, unattended
# and past its gate. `boot_resume.ran_here` refuses that too; this is the first
# of the two locks.
runs/**/inflight.json
runs/**/inflight.json.tmp
runs/.boot-resume.lock
# Same reasoning for the trainer watch: `quiet_since` and `last_action` describe
# processes on THIS box. Restored into a fresh clone they would either suppress
# a rescue (a `last_action` from another machine reads as a cooldown) or invent
# an hour-old absence that never happened here.
runs/.train-watch.json
runs/.train-watch.json.tmp
runs/.train-watch.lock
runs/.train-watch-stall-issue
# Machine-local network counter baseline. A stale one restored into a fresh
# clone would report a wrong egress delta on a box that never sent those bytes.
runs/.egress-baseline.json

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# dataprep progress logs
data/*_progress.jsonl*
